.TH SIFTICS\-SETUP 1 "2026-05-31" "SIFTics 0.1" "SIFTics Manual"
.SH NAME
siftics\-setup \- one\-shot installer and launcher for the SIFTics IR agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./setup.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setup.sh
is the express installer for SIFTics on a SANS SIFT Workstation or any
Ubuntu/Debian host.
It is fully idempotent \(em re\-running is safe and skips steps that have
already completed.
.PP
The script performs up to seven steps, depending on flags:
.TP
1.
Check system prerequisites (Python\ 3.10+, curl, venv/ensurepip).
.TP
2.
Create a Python virtual environment at
.IR .venv/ .
.TP
3.
Install Python dependencies (Flask, MCP SDK, Anthropic SDK, etc.)
via
.BR pip\ install\ -e\ . .
.TP
4.
Seed or build the Rathbun known\-good Windows baseline database.
.TP
5.
\fI(optional)\fR Initialise a case directory with a hash\-chained audit log,
IC HMAC key, and 35\-question Initial Triage Questionnaire.
.TP
6.
\fI(optional)\fR Launch the SIFTics web UI on port 8080.
.TP
7.
Build the forensic\-RAG knowledge index at
.IR mcp_rag/index/ ,
if not already present.
Clones and indexes from GitHub sources (~10\(en30\ min, network\-bound).
If the build fails, setup warns but does not abort.
Skip with
.BR \-\-no\-rag .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Baseline DB
Mutually exclusive. Default: seed a ~50\-row demo baseline (instant).
.TP
.B \-\-full\-baseline
Download the full ~100\ MB Rathbun DB from the latest GitHub Release
(~30\ s, requires network).
.TP
.B \-\-build\-baseline
Build the full DB locally from Rathbun sources
(~30\ min, ~5\ GB disk cache, requires git and network).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-baseline
Skip the baseline step entirely.
.SS Forensic-RAG index
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rag
Skip Step\ 7 (forensic\-RAG index build).
Use this flag when the index at
.I mcp_rag/index/
is already present, when running offline, or when disk space is limited.
Without the index,
.B mcp_rag
falls back to a hash\-bag embedder (functional but lower\-quality semantic search).
.SS Case initialisation
.TP
.B \-\-init\-case
Create the case directory, hash\-chained audit log, IC HMAC key, and seed
the 35\-question ITQ template.
.TP
.BI \-\-case\-dir " DIR"
Path to the case directory.
Default:
.IR ~/Desktop/cases/dry_run .
Overrides
.BR $SIFTICS_CASE_DIR .
.TP
.BI \-\-case\-id " ID"
Case identifier string embedded in
.IR case.json .
Default:
.BI dry_run_ YYYYMMDD .
.SS AI runtimes
If none of the runtime flags are passed and the session has a TTY, an
interactive prompt asks which runtimes to install. Node.js is installed
automatically if required.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-claude
Install Claude Code CLI via npm
.RB ( @anthropic-ai/claude-code ).
Recommended — this is the primary agentic runtime SIFTics was built for.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-codex
Install OpenAI Codex CLI via npm
.RB ( @openai/codex ).
.TP
.B \-\-install\-ollama
Install Ollama local LLM server (no API key required).
After installation, pull a model with
.BR "ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:32b" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-runtimes
Skip the interactive runtime prompt and install nothing.
Use this for CI or repeated re-runs.
.SS Web UI
.TP
.B \-\-start\-ui
Launch
.B siftics\-ui
on port 8080 after setup completes. Binds to
.B 0.0.0.0
so the dashboard is reachable from a host browser at
.BI http:// <vm\-ip> :8080 .
Available pages:
.BR /dashboard ,
.BR /gates ,
.BR /audit ,
.BR /chat ,
.BR /setup ,
.BR /report ,
.BR /findings ,
.BR /intel .
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress verbose pip output; only final status lines are printed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Express path \(em everything in one command:
.B ./setup.sh \-\-init\-case \-\-start\-ui
.TP
Full baseline, custom case directory:
.B ./setup.sh \-\-full\-baseline \-\-init\-case \-\-case\-dir ~/Desktop/cases/defcon2019 \-\-case\-id defcon2019 \-\-start\-ui
.TP
Headless / CI (no TTY, IC key creation skipped):
.B ./setup.sh \-\-no\-baseline \-\-init\-case
.TP
Re\-run after partial install (safe):
.B ./setup.sh \-\-start\-ui
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .venv/
Python virtual environment created by the script.
.TP
.I mcp_baseline/baseline.sqlite
Rathbun known\-good Windows baseline database.
.TP
.I ~/Desktop/cases/<case\-id>/
Case directory containing
.IR case.json ,
.IR forensic_audit.jsonl ,
.IR findings.jsonl ,
.IR intel.jsonl ,
.IR ic_key.hmac ,
and the ASR/CET/ITQ JSONL registers.
.TP
.I mcp_rag/index/
Forensic\-RAG SQLite\-vec index (6,337 records: Sigma, ATT&CK, Atomic Red Team, LOLBAS).
Built automatically by Step\ 7 on first run.
Rebuild manually with
.BR "./scripts/download_rag_index.sh \-\-build" .
.TP
.I /tmp/siftics\-ui.log
Web UI stdout/stderr (tail with
.BR "tail \-F /tmp/siftics\-ui.log" ).
.TP
.I /tmp/siftics_*.log
Per\-step log files written during baseline build and case initialisation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIFTICS_CASE_DIR
If set, used as the default case directory when
.B \-\-case\-dir
is not supplied.
.SH INSTALLATION
To install this man page system\-wide:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cp docs/man/siftics\-setup.1 /usr/local/man/man1/
.br
.B sudo mandb
.RE
.PP
Then access with:
.B man siftics\-setup
